em. It provides no significant visual treatment other than to provide indication for the user to take a common action."},"115":{"id":"/docs/components/button-17","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."},"116":{"id":"/docs/components/button-18","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."},"117":{"id":"/docs/components/button-19","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."},"118":{"id":"/docs/components/button-20","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"The critical button signifies to the user a destructive action will take place."},"119":{"id":"/docs/components/button-21","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Any button variant can be disabled to prevent interaction, communicated with reduced opacity and a not-allowed cursor."},"120":{"id":"/docs/components/button-22","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"You may provide an optional `Icon` component to the button. If you do not include text, you must provide an aria-label attribute to identify the purpose of the button. This will produce a square button."},"121":{"id":"/docs/components/button-23","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#inline","content":"The inline button sits within a run of text, styled like a link while retaining button semantics."},"122":{"id":"/docs